    "body": "@smhigley just reminded me that this might get a little interesting with accessibility API mapping, since in some screen readers a [modal dialog](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/#att-open-dialog) doesn't let a screen reader user move their virtual cursor outside of it once they are in it, regardless of whatever else is going on with the accessibility tree. So we might need to take extra care with the mappings for those APIs, and move other top layer nodes inside the dialog in the accessibility tree to ensure that they can be accessed.\r\n\r\n@jcsteh may have thoughts on how feasible this is; I'm less familiar with the APIs where this occurs. From a browser internals perspective I believe this should be manageable; it would be equivalent to using `aria-owns` to append those elements to the end of the dialog.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
