    "body": "Another approach to this problem, though probably not a workable one, might be to prevent elements outside the “blocking” top layer element from forming another non-blocking top layer on top of it. i.e., if your popover element is outside the dialog, it simply doesn’t get to be rendered on top of it.\r\n\r\nThis would probably be considered a breaking change from the perspective of sighted non screen reader users, since it would change the behaviour of popovers for those users. It would also require more re-tooling of pages converting from pre-popover code which placed to-be popover elements at the end of the document as a kind of top layer hack, as described by Scott’s original problem statement.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
