    "updated_at": "2024-12-19T23:17:34Z",
    "body": "Right, I misspoke a little originally: I meant that things in the *top* top layer should generally not be inert. A popover is always “in the top layer”, but if it’s below a blocking top layer like a dialog, then it’s not in the *top* top layer. You could certainly have multiple top layers of popover which should all be non-inert, too, so it’s more complex than just “which top layer is on top”, but as an intuition, I would expect the very top layer certainly shouldn’t be inert.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
