    "created_at": "2025-03-31T17:23:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-31T17:23:36Z",
    "body": "> [@smhigley](https://github.com/smhigley) just reminded me that this might get a little interesting with accessibility API mapping, since in some screen readers a [modal dialog](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/#att-open-dialog) doesn't let a screen reader user move their virtual cursor outside of it once they are in it, regardless of whatever else is going on with the accessibility tree. So we might need to take extra care with the mappings for those APIs, and move other top layer nodes inside the dialog in the accessibility tree to ensure that they can be accessed.\n> \n> [@jcsteh](https://github.com/jcsteh) may have thoughts on how feasible this is; I'm less familiar with the APIs where this occurs. From a browser internals perspective I believe this should be manageable; it would be equivalent to using `aria-owns` to append those elements to the end of the dialog.\n\nI was talking to @aleventhal about this last week, and he reminded me that popovers already have `aria-details` relationships between the triggering button and the popover. His feeling was that perhaps this means that a full `aria-owns` relationship wouldn't be necessary, and might even be too much for this case? What do you both think?\n\nIf the above is true, then the change being proposed here would be:\n\n1. If there's a modal `<dialog>` (call it \"M\") open on the page, then all non-modal top-layer elements (call them \"TL\") that come *after*  M will also be de-inerted.\n2. Only the last modal `<dialog>` in the top layer stack gets de-inerted. I.e. if there are two modal dialogs open, only the last one (plus follow-on TL elements) is de-inerted.\n3. If there is already an `aria-details` relationship between M and each of the TL elements, no further a11y tree changes are necessary. If not, an `aria-owns` should be added, pointing from M to each of the TLs. I don't know what to do if some TLs are `aria-details` targets and some aren't.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
