    "created_at": "2025-04-11T14:35:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-11T17:22:05Z",
    "body": "@mfreed7 i don't think the aria-details association between the button and the popover will hit all of the use cases for popovers being invoked outside of modal dialogs.\n\nThe most pressing use case being the notification/alert/toast use case where those popovers will likely (should) be manual and rendered via scripting.  \n\n\neven for that use case - if the notification didn't become 'owned' by the dialog, there will be instances where even if it became uninerted but remained outside of the dialog, a user could still never come across it.\n\nfor instance, there are two ways to make a live region notification that will have the highest likelihood of working with the different screen reader and browser combinations:\n1. create an empty live region and then populate content into it as needed, removing old text/content when done.\n2. injecting elements with role=alert into the document.  not always the best choice, but no need to get into that now.\n\nso, people (who are at least trying to make notifications accessible) will be doing one of those two practices.\n\nThe issue with 1 is that if the popover is what's made inert, it won't be live region content anymore since that container element will still be part of the inert document.  So the content will show up, but it won't be announced.\n\n2 will be far better, though the problem with not having the dialog own this popover is that while it will at least be announced as a live region, screen readers like JAWS and NVDA make a point to at least partially limit virtual cursor navigation to dialogs.  So, if the alert is still outside of the dialog, a user can hear it, they might even try to navigate to it with the virtual cursor - but depending on how it's built, they may still not be able to directly access it.\n\nsimilar to alice, i mocked up an example to try and illustrate the above. \nhttps://codepen.io/scottohara/full/OPJKPpo\n\ni highly doubt developers will know to do the aria-own-ing themselves.  Nor, do I think they'll know that they will need to un-own the popovers when a dialog is dismissed (with safari, for instance, that would result in the owned popovers being completely inaccessible because the dialog is removed from the a11y tree in the hidden state.)\n\nsorry again for the long comment.... i hope this was at least helpful in outlining this particular use case more.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
